DS605 Lab Assignment 7: Image Representation, PCA, Eigenfaces and Face Recognition

Overview
This project explores PCA and eigenfaces for dimensionality reduction, image reconstruction, and face recognition using the AT&T ORL Face Database. 
PCA is implemented from scratch using NumPy linear-algebra operations.

Dataset
The ORL dataset contains 400 grayscale face images from 40 subjects, with 10 images per subject. Each image has dimensions of 112 × 92 pixels. 
The dataset is divided into: Training set: 70% and Testing set: 30%.  Each subject is represented in both sets.

Methodology
•	Load grayscale images and convert them into numerical feature vectors.
•	Calculate the mean face and center the training data.
•	Implement PCA using covariance-based eigendecomposition and SVD.
•	Analyze cumulative explained variance and select components preserving at least 90% variance.
•	Visualize eigenfaces and reconstruct sample face images.
•	Compare raw-pixel and PCA-based nearest-neighbor recognition using Euclidean distance.
•	Train and evaluate KNN, Logistic Regression, and SVM classifiers using PCA features.
•	Compare recognition accuracy, reconstruction quality, and storage requirements.

Results
The notebook generates explained-variance plots, eigenface visualizations, reconstructed face examples, recognition comparisons, and CSV files containing experimental 
results.

Conclusion
This project demonstrates how PCA can reduce the dimensionality of face images while retaining important information. It compares covariance-based PCA with SVD and 
evaluates similarity-based face recognition against traditional machine-learning classifiers. The experiments investigate the relationship between dimensionality, 
storage efficiency, reconstruction quality, and recognition accuracy.
